-- Dispatch-role background workers stay dormant while
-- whpg_dispatch_topology_file is set.
--
-- FTS, dtx recovery and the global deadlock detector never run while the
-- postmaster is in recovery; they start the moment recovery ends, and FTS
-- probes (dtx recovery dispatches) before the first sleep.  On a
-- coordinator whose catalog is not authoritative (a dispatch topology file
-- is in effect) they would act on the catalog's stale addresses.  The gate
-- (dispatch_topology_bgworker_gated) makes FTS skip its whole probe cycle
-- -- catalog read, gpsegconfig_dump, status version, probe -- keeps the
-- loop's counters moving, holds dtx recovery before recoverTM() (so
-- *shmDtmStarted stays unset and dispatch connections are refused), and
-- resumes both on clear + reload.
--
-- The scenario is driven on the suite's standby coordinator: set the GUC
-- there, promote it (the only way to get a coordinator with the GUC set out
-- of recovery), watch the workers start gated, clear the GUC, watch them
-- wake.  The standby is destroyed and re-created at the end.
--
-- BLAST RADIUS -- this test must stay last in the schedule and must never
-- run concurrently with anything: the promoted node is a clone of the
-- coordinator, so once its gate lifts its dtx recovery dispatches into this
-- cluster's live primaries: gp_terminate_mpp_backends() (every QE of every
-- session) and ROLLBACK PREPARED of every prepared transaction it does not
-- know.  While the gate holds none of that happens, which is what the
-- first half asserts; the second half deliberately lets it happen while
-- nothing else is running.  Not observable here: the deadlock detector
-- (off in gpdemo, and it waits for the DTM the gate keeps unstarted) and
-- the autovacuum launcher's gate (autovacuum is off in this suite).
--
-- Sessions: 1: primary QD; -1S: standby QD (dispatch); -1M: standby QD in
-- utility mode.  The fts_probe fault is only reached by an un-gated FTS
-- cycle, so its hit count is the proof that no probe was attempted; as a
-- 'skip' it also keeps a woken FTS from really probing this cluster's
-- primaries.  ftsLoop_topology_gated / dtx_recovery_topology_gated count
-- the gated cycles of the two workers.  The faults live in the promoted
-- node's shared memory and die with it, so they are never reset.

-- Stage the topology file: the role='m' rows are what a hot-standby QD
-- dispatches to (plus itself for content -1).  Set the GUC on the standby
-- only, with a short probe interval, and record a mtime reference for the
-- configuration dump file.
!\retcode sdir=$(psql -X -d postgres -Atc "select datadir from gp_segment_configuration where content = -1 and role = 'm'"); psql -X -At -d postgres -c "select content, dbid, hostname, address, port, datadir from gp_segment_configuration where role = 'm' order by content" | tr '|' ' ' > "$sdir/whpg_fts_gate_topology" && echo "whpg_dispatch_topology_file = 'whpg_fts_gate_topology'" >> "$sdir/postgresql.conf" && echo "gp_fts_probe_interval = 10" >> "$sdir/postgresql.conf" && touch "$sdir/hs_fts_gate_marker" && pg_ctl reload -D "$sdir";
-- start_ignore
server signaled

-- end_ignore
(exited with code 0)

